.TH WIMM 1 "" "where-is-my-memory" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wimm \- see what uses memory, CPU and disk, and reclaim it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wimm
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.RB [ \-\-group = \fIID\fR ]
.br
.B wimm status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B wimm \-\-version
.br
.B wimm \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wimm
is the command that starts where-is-my-memory, a GTK4 application that shows
which processes, containers and projects use memory, CPU and disk, and lets the
user close or clean them after an explicit confirmation.
.PP
The application is a single resident process with a tray icon.
Running
.B wimm
again does not start a second copy: the running instance opens its window.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Start without opening the window.
The window still opens on the first run, and when no tray host is available to
show the icon.
.TP
.BI \-\-group= ID
Show the group with the given identifier.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the list of options and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print the current state on the terminal, without a window and without GTK, so
it also works over SSH.
The data comes from the running instance when there is one; otherwise
.B wimm
takes a single sampling cycle in the calling process.
.TP
.B status \-\-json
Print the same state as JSON.
Names, paths and password aliases are redacted, as in the snapshot the running
instance exposes on D-Bus.
.PP
Exit status of
.BR "wimm status" :
.TP
.B 0
The state was printed.
.TP
.B 3
No state is available: there is no running instance and the system could not be
read.
The reason goes to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/where-is-my-memory/
Preferences (\fIconfig.json\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/where-is-my-memory/
Saved state (\fIstate.json\fR, \fIwindow.json\fR), the first-run marker
(\fIwelcomed\fR) and the rotating log (\fIwimm.log\fR).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/where-is-my-memory/
Disk scan cache (\fIdisk\-cache.json\fR), safe to delete.
.PP
The three directories follow the XDG variables
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
and
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME ,
and are created with mode 0700.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WIMM_LOG_LEVEL
Log level: one of DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR or CRITICAL, case-insensitive.
The default is INFO; an invalid value is reported in the log and INFO is used.
.PP
.B WIMM_APP_ID
also selects the instance that
.B wimm status
talks to.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1),
.BR docker (1)
